WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.840 --> 00:00:02.430
- [Narrator] Fast casual chain Cava

00:00:02.430 --> 00:00:04.080
has turned Mediterranean dishes

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:07.260
into a nearly $4 billion business.

00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:10.620
But most of its growth came
from an uncommon strategy:

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:12.750
buying a competitor quadruple its size

00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:15.260
and converting all its
locations into Cavas.

00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:17.010
(lively music)

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:19.500
- I like to say I went to bed
running about 70 restaurants

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:22.260
and woke up running over 250 restaurants.

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:23.880
- [Narrator] The strategy: turn Cava

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:26.970
into the country's biggest
Mediterranean restaurant chain,

00:00:26.970 --> 00:00:28.350
leaving many to compare it

00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:30.840
to where Chipotle was a decade ago.

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:33.780
Its success depends on how
long the Mediterranean diet

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:35.460
can remain popular.

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:38.070
The company says it's
using lots of customer data

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:41.160
to strategize where to open new locations,

00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:44.040
but now that Cava can no
longer rely on an acquisition

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:45.930
to scale up, how can it continue

00:00:45.930 --> 00:00:47.910
to grow at such an ambitious pace?

00:00:47.910 --> 00:00:51.270
- Growth takes time, it's
expensive, it's variable,

00:00:51.270 --> 00:00:54.750
and I think that's a little
bit of coming down to reality.

00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:57.537
- [Narrator] This is
"The Economics of Cava."

00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:02.190
Cava has been rapidly expanding for years.

00:01:02.190 --> 00:01:03.840
- Cava really likes the suburbs.

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:05.610
They really see potential there,

00:01:05.610 --> 00:01:06.900
and some of those communities

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:10.200
probably don't have other
Mediterranean food options

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:14.520
or readily, you know,
marketed to them options

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:15.690
that they might seek out.

00:01:15.690 --> 00:01:18.450
- We've built a really
robust real estate model

00:01:18.450 --> 00:01:22.140
that includes demographic
and psychographic analysis

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:26.730
and we then use mobile
analytics to understand

00:01:26.730 --> 00:01:29.130
where our guests are coming
from, where they're going,

00:01:29.130 --> 00:01:31.950
and then kind of create
a DNA of our guest base,

00:01:31.950 --> 00:01:34.440
and then heat map that
DNA across the country

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:35.400
to then show us

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:37.740
where we have the highest
likelihood of success.

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:40.620
- [Narrator] In 2018,
Cava bought Zoe's Kitchen,

00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:43.290
another chain of fast casual
Mediterranean restaurants,

00:01:43.290 --> 00:01:45.120
for $300 million.

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:48.960
At the time, Zoe's Kitchen
had 261 locations compared

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:51.060
to Cava's more than 70,

00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:53.850
but Zoe's kitchen was
burning through cash.

00:01:53.850 --> 00:01:55.050
- It was a melting ice cube

00:01:55.050 --> 00:01:57.270
and we didn't want it
to turn into a puddle.

00:01:57.270 --> 00:01:59.130
- [Narrator] Zoe's Kitchen, Schulman said,

00:01:59.130 --> 00:02:00.450
had lost its identity,

00:02:00.450 --> 00:02:02.940
serving as a cautionary tale for Cava.

00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:06.630
- I think over time,
Zoe's had lost its focus.

00:02:06.630 --> 00:02:08.550
It had added many menu items.

00:02:08.550 --> 00:02:10.710
I think the consumer was kind of confused

00:02:10.710 --> 00:02:12.720
as to what the brand really stood for

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:15.810
and what their core
competency is versus at Cava,

00:02:15.810 --> 00:02:18.360
we're really about these
modern Mediterranean flavors.

00:02:18.360 --> 00:02:22.380
38 ingredients, very
simple, focused operation.

00:02:22.380 --> 00:02:24.450
- [Narrator] Most of the
new restaurants Cava opened

00:02:24.450 --> 00:02:27.060
from 2019 to 2023 came

00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:29.940
from converting existing
Zoe's Kitchen locations.

00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:33.090
This meant Cava could scale
faster and at half the cost

00:02:33.090 --> 00:02:35.460
of building new restaurants from scratch.

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:37.560
- When we looked at the
Zoe's real estate portfolio,

00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:40.920
we saw many sites across the
portfolio that we would love

00:02:40.920 --> 00:02:42.900
as a Cava site that we felt

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:44.850
was really underperforming its potential.

00:02:44.850 --> 00:02:46.590
So we felt like this would be a way

00:02:46.590 --> 00:02:49.950
to rapidly expand our brand in a part

00:02:49.950 --> 00:02:52.380
of the country we were
trying to enter into.

00:02:52.380 --> 00:02:54.870
And we could do it in a much faster way

00:02:54.870 --> 00:02:57.780
than if we were trying to
source these deals one by one.

00:02:57.780 --> 00:02:59.970
- [Narrator] Cava converted
its last Zoe's Kitchen

00:02:59.970 --> 00:03:02.880
in October 2023, which means that now

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:05.970
it has to build new
locations from the ground up.

00:03:05.970 --> 00:03:09.780
Cava is currently in 24
states, plus Washington, D.C.,

00:03:09.780 --> 00:03:12.330
and it went public in June 2023.

00:03:12.330 --> 00:03:14.070
As it looks to grow, it hopes

00:03:14.070 --> 00:03:16.290
to capitalize on the rising popularity

00:03:16.290 --> 00:03:18.990
of the Mediterranean diet,
which it hopes to appeal

00:03:18.990 --> 00:03:22.020
to a broad range of
customers across the country.

00:03:22.020 --> 00:03:23.760
Right now, only 1.4%

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:27.690
of US restaurants primarily
serve Mediterranean cuisine.

00:03:27.690 --> 00:03:29.220
In its last quarterly report,

00:03:29.220 --> 00:03:33.210
Cava Group reported a net
income of $6.8 million

00:03:33.210 --> 00:03:37.140
with a restaurant level
profit margin of 25.1%.

00:03:37.140 --> 00:03:39.860
Cava is now the largest
Mediterranean style restaurant chain

00:03:39.860 --> 00:03:42.600
in the country, but is
it the next Chipotle?

00:03:42.600 --> 00:03:46.530
- Chipotle was really
taking Mexican nationwide

00:03:46.530 --> 00:03:47.790
in a very unique way

00:03:47.790 --> 00:03:51.630
that's an assembly line style
of creating burritos and bowls

00:03:51.630 --> 00:03:56.370
and Cava is seeking to take
Mediterranean food nationwide

00:03:56.370 --> 00:03:58.260
with also kind of more
of an assembly line,

00:03:58.260 --> 00:04:01.290
fast casual style of service.

00:04:01.290 --> 00:04:03.090
But Chipotle was getting going

00:04:03.090 --> 00:04:05.700
when fast casual really was barely a blip.

00:04:05.700 --> 00:04:07.890
So there was a lot less competition then.

00:04:07.890 --> 00:04:10.110
Cava has a lot more competition now.

00:04:10.110 --> 00:04:11.850
- [Narrator] Whether
the restaurant succeeds

00:04:11.850 --> 00:04:14.520
may largely depend on
whether customers continue

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:16.260
to seek Mediterranean food.

00:04:16.260 --> 00:04:18.450
- Mediterranean has gotten
a lot of good buzz, right?

00:04:18.450 --> 00:04:20.910
It's seen as healthier,
it's good for the heart

00:04:20.910 --> 00:04:22.860
and you know, overall body.

00:04:22.860 --> 00:04:24.150
That said, it's still new.

00:04:24.150 --> 00:04:27.360
Harissa, tahini, falafel,
for a lot of communities,

00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:30.090
these are still new kinds of foods

00:04:30.090 --> 00:04:31.920
and that's still a question mark.

00:04:31.920 --> 00:04:33.960
Do people wanna eat
this day in and day out

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:35.370
as opposed to just trying it?

00:04:35.370 --> 00:04:37.230
- As of October 2023,

00:04:37.230 --> 00:04:40.080
Cava finished converting
all Zoe's kitchen locations

00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:42.540
into Cavas but it's told investors

00:04:42.540 --> 00:04:44.940
that it will continue growing
its number of locations

00:04:44.940 --> 00:04:47.340
by at least 15% each year.

00:04:47.340 --> 00:04:50.010
- I think the biggest question
is can they grow in the way

00:04:50.010 --> 00:04:51.810
that they've said that they're going to

00:04:51.810 --> 00:04:54.360
for their investors,
and do it organically?

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:57.120
Now they have to open their own
sites, find their own sites,

00:04:57.120 --> 00:05:00.510
make sure the sites are good,
be able to afford paying

00:05:00.510 --> 00:05:03.180
for this real estate and
construction costs and other costs.

00:05:03.180 --> 00:05:04.200
- [Narrator] It plans to open

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:06.060
at least three restaurants in Chicago,

00:05:06.060 --> 00:05:08.940
which will be its first
major foray into the Midwest.

00:05:08.940 --> 00:05:12.870
It's targeting 47 to 50
new restaurants in 2024

00:05:12.870 --> 00:05:15.090
with locations based
on a significant amount

00:05:15.090 --> 00:05:16.320
of customer data.

00:05:16.320 --> 00:05:19.110
- I think restaurants are
a blend of art and science,

00:05:19.110 --> 00:05:20.820
and so we love the science part

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:23.040
and understanding how do we use data

00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:24.810
to inform our decisions?

00:05:24.810 --> 00:05:27.570
So it gives us great
visibility into being able

00:05:27.570 --> 00:05:30.660
to take this brand to the 26
states we're not in today,

00:05:30.660 --> 00:05:32.190
and to go broader and deeper

00:05:32.190 --> 00:05:35.340
in the 24 states we already
currently operate in.

00:05:35.340 --> 00:05:36.570
- [Narrator] But it's a difficult time

00:05:36.570 --> 00:05:39.150
to be expanding a fast casual restaurant.

00:05:39.150 --> 00:05:40.740
The economic slowdown has led

00:05:40.740 --> 00:05:42.630
to many restaurants struggling,

00:05:42.630 --> 00:05:45.060
and while chain establishments
are better positioned

00:05:45.060 --> 00:05:48.300
than independent ones,
the market is saturated.

00:05:48.300 --> 00:05:50.250
Despite this, Cava is planning

00:05:50.250 --> 00:05:53.910
for a 15% growth in
store numbers next year.

00:05:53.910 --> 00:05:58.440
- If you look at where US-based
restaurant chains are now,

00:05:58.440 --> 00:06:00.300
I mean, Wingstop, which is mentioned

00:06:00.300 --> 00:06:04.467
as the big growth engine
is at something like 11%,

00:06:04.467 --> 00:06:06.750
and I believe Cava is
projecting even more.

00:06:06.750 --> 00:06:08.910
So they have grown very quickly

00:06:08.910 --> 00:06:12.330
and they've really promised
more growth at a very high rate.

00:06:12.330 --> 00:06:13.860
And so investors are gonna be looking

00:06:13.860 --> 00:06:15.444
for those numbers every year.

00:06:15.444 --> 00:06:18.111
(lively music)

